{
    "info": {
        "name": "L09ClientMCP - MCP Client Demo",
        "description": "Educational API collection for demonstrating MCP Client functionality.\n\nThis collection shows the evolution from basic chatbot to MCP-enabled AI application.\n\n**Prerequisites:**\n- Application running on localhost:8080\n- OPENAI_API_KEY environment variable set\n- For MCP testing: Start with `mcp-stdio` profile\n\n**Branch 3 Updates:**\n- Added MCP status, tools, and invocation endpoints\n- Echo server demonstration capabilities\n- Tool discovery and testing features\n\n**Learning Objectives:**\n- Understand REST API design for AI applications\n- See how chatbot responses evolve with MCP integration\n- Practice API testing methodologies\n- Experience MCP tool discovery and invocation",
        "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
    },
    "item": [
        {
            "name": "Health Check",
            "event": [
                {
                    "listen": "test",
                    "script": {
                        "exec": [
                            "pm.test('Health check returns 200', function () {",
                            "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                            "});",
                            "",
                            "pm.test('Response contains expected message', function () {",
                            "    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.include('Chat service is running');",
                            "});",
                            "",
                            "pm.test('Response includes MCP status', function () {",
                            "    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.include('MCP:');",
                            "});",
                            "",
                            "// Extract and log MCP status for educational purposes",
                            "const responseText = pm.response.text();",
                            "const mcpMatch = responseText.match(/MCP: (\\w+) \\(([^)]+)\\)/);",
                            "if (mcpMatch) {",
                            "    console.log('✅ Service is healthy and ready for chat requests');",
                            "    console.log('🔧 MCP Status: ' + mcpMatch[1] + ' - ' + mcpMatch[2]);",
                            "} else {",
                            "    console.log('✅ Service is healthy and ready for chat requests');",
                            "    console.log('ℹ️  MCP status format may have changed');",
                            "}"
                        ],
                        "type": "text/javascript"
                    }
                }
            ],
            "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                    "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/chat/health",
                    "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
                    "path": ["api", "chat", "health"]
                },
                "description": "**Purpose:** Verify the application is running and healthy.\n\n**What to expect:**\n- Status: 200 OK\n- Response: \"Chat service is running. MCP: healthy (status details)\"\n\n**Branch 2+ Changes:**\n- Now includes MCP (Model Context Protocol) status\n- Shows whether MCP is enabled/disabled\n- Displays MCP configuration details\n\n**Teaching Points:**\n- Health checks are essential for monitoring\n- MCP status helps debug configuration issues\n- Foundation for more complex API testing\n- Shows system architecture evolution"
            },
            "response": []
        },
